90 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 76 0 R
/E (Muscle gain, or muscle hypertrophy, is the process by which muscles increase in size and strength in response to specific stimuli such as resistance training and proper nutrition. It begins with resistance training, which causes microscopic damage to muscle fibers, triggering an inflammatory response and activating satellite cells for repair and regeneration. Protein synthesis is elevated to repair the damaged fibers and promote muscle growth, facilitated by adequate nutrition, particularly protein intake. Rest and recovery are essential for muscle gain, allowing the body time to repair and adapt to the training stimulus. Progressive overload, achieved by gradually increasing workout intensity, volume, or resistance, stimulates further muscle growth over time. By consistently engaging in resistance training, maintaining proper nutrition, prioritizing rest, and progressively overloading the muscles, individuals can optimize the process of muscle gain and achieve their strength and physique goals.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
91 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 76 0 R
/T (How does Muscle Gain successfully happen?)
/E (How does Muscle Gain successfully happen?)
