103 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 80 0 R
/E (To effectively support muscle gain, it's crucial to focus on a balanced diet that provides the necessary nutrients for muscle repair and growth. Aim to consume a diet rich in lean proteins, complex carbohydrates, and healthy fats. Include protein sources such as chicken, turkey, fish, lean beef, eggs, dairy products, tofu, legumes, and protein supplements. Carbohydrates are essential for providing energy during workouts and replenishing glycogen stores, so incorporate whole grains, fruits, vegetables, and starchy vegetables into your meals. Healthy fats, found in foods like nuts, seeds, avocados, and olive oil, support hormone production and overall health. Eat regular meals and snacks throughout the day to maintain a steady supply of nutrients for muscle growth, and stay hydrated by drinking plenty of water. Finally, consider timing your meals around workouts to optimize performance and recovery, consuming a balanced meal containing protein and carbohydrates before and after exercise.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
